# SUPERCOMPUTE — Cloudflare Pages headers
# Static export output (public/ -> out/ on build).
#
# CLOUDFLARE SYNTAX: headers only apply inside a path section. A block with no
# path line ("/*" or "/path") is silently ignored — the previous revision of this
# file was written that way, so none of it ever reached a browser. Everything in
# the /* section below is therefore in effect for the FIRST time. Treat it as a
# fresh rollout, not a tweak.
#
# COEP require-corp was declared in that dead block and is intentionally NOT
# re-added: it would block cross-origin images/media that lack CORP headers.
#
# CSP <-> transport invariant (kept honest in BOTH directions):
#   Browser-side RPC transports are defined in lib/web3.ts and every one of them
#   MUST be listed in connect-src below:
#     base    -> https://mainnet.base.org   (viem's Base default)
#     mainnet -> https://eth.drpc.org
#   Both are pinned explicitly in lib/web3.ts so this stays a static mapping. A
#   bare http() would resolve to chain.rpcUrls.default.http[0] at request time:
#   for mainnet that is https://eth.merkle.io, which 429s (Cloudflare error 1015)
#   under ordinary traffic, so mainnet is pinned to a host that answers reads.
#
#   The other mainnet RPC hosts in the repo (functions/api/auth.js,
#   functions/api/web3/[[catchall]].js, functions/api/token.js) are Cloudflare
#   Pages Functions: server-side, where CSP does not apply. They deliberately do
#   NOT appear here — listing a host the browser never contacts makes the policy
#   lie about its own trust surface, and none of them work from a browser anyway
#   (llamarpc/publicnode fail the TLS handshake, cloudflare-eth.com cannot serve
#   eth_blockNumber). Adding a browser-side read against any of them requires
#   adding it below first.
#
# COOP: same-origin is in effect for the first time. No live impact today — the
# only window.open() is components/FiatRamp.tsx:62, which already passes
# "noopener", and the WalletConnect modal is an iframe. If a popup-based flow is
# ever added (OAuth / social login / Coinbase), COOP MUST become
# same-origin-allow-popups or that popup loses window.opener.
#
# X-Frame-Options is SAMEORIGIN, aligned with frame-ancestors 'self'. It was DENY,
# which contradicted the CSP: modern browsers honour frame-ancestors and ignore
# XFO, older ones let DENY win — so same-origin framing silently broke on older
# browsers. SAMEORIGIN keeps the legacy clickjacking protection and agrees with
# the CSP instead of removing the header.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; img-src 'self' data: https:; font-src 'self' data: https://fonts.gstatic.com; connect-src 'self' https://api.neynar.com https://fonts.gstatic.com https://mainnet.base.org https://eth.drpc.org https://*.walletconnect.com https://*.walletconnect.org wss://*.walletconnect.com wss://*.walletconnect.org; media-src 'self' blob: https:; worker-src 'self' blob:; frame-src 'self' https://*.walletconnect.com https://*.walletconnect.org https://www.youtube.com https://calendly.com; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()

# Immutable hashed build assets
/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.woff2
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.jpg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.jpeg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.webp
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# HTML — never cache stale
/*.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
